@@ -2,6 +2,52 @@
 title: Qwen3.6 MoE
 description: Launch recipe for Qwen3.6-35B-A3B with MTP training and EAGLE speculative rollout.
 ---
+
+## Disaggregated B200 agentic-RL benchmark
+
+`scripts/run_qwen3_6_35b_a3b_posttrainingx.py` combines this model recipe with
+the fully asynchronous OpenEnv control flow. It requires four eight-GPU B200
+nodes and an external, run-owned Ray cluster. It never starts or kills shared
+Ray, Miles, SGLang, or Redis processes.
+
+The `--layout` choices are `1t3r`, `2t2r`, and `3t1r`. Each rollout node hosts
+one EP8 engine. The trainer retains TP1/EP8/CP1/PP1/ETP1 and the cookbook MTP,
+optimizer, and recomputation settings. It uses broadcast weight updates at
+interval one, staleness one, and sample-granularity submission. `retract` is
+the initial pause mode. Select `--pause-generation-mode in_place` only after
+the broadcast activation test passes.
+
+This is a benchmark implementation awaiting GPU validation, not a qualified
+performance recipe. Supply pinned checkpoints and clean Terminal-Lego or TMAX
+prompt data. Terminal-Bench 2.1 is reserved for separate offline evaluation.
+The launcher does not install packages, download benchmark tasks, assert
+checkpoint/resume fidelity, or bypass the environment-isolation gate.
+
+```bash
+python scripts/run_qwen3_6_35b_a3b_posttrainingx.py \
+    --hardware B200 --layout 2t2r --execution async \
+    --output-dir /shared/posttrainingx/runs/vultr-b200-slurm \
+    --run-id example --model-dir /shared/posttrainingx/runs/vultr-b200-slurm/example/models \
+    --openenv-env-url http://ENV_CONTROLLER:8003 --num-rollout 400
+```
+
+Use `--execution sync --num-rollout 3` for the optimizer correctness test. The
+site adapter must validate inventory, assets, environment isolation, and
+serving first. `--host-map` points at a JSON object with `schema_version: 1`
+and a `nodes` list. Each node supplies `hostname`, numeric IPv4 `ray_node_ip`,
+`role` (`trainer` or `rollout`), and all eight physical `gpu_uuids`. List trainer
+nodes first, then rollout nodes. Rotate that order to rotate physical roles.
+Ray placement is rejected if a host or physical GPU differs from the map.
+For a resume launch, provide a new `--placement-record-path` so the previous
+placement record remains immutable.
+
+The optimizer budget defaults to 400 steps with saves every 50 steps. This
+does not guarantee a quality improvement. Evaluation budgets and the final
+comparison must be pre-registered independently of Terminal-Bench outcomes.
+Megatron's dense-parameter DP and expert DP are distinct quantities. With TP1,
+dense DP has one rank per trainer GPU, while expert DP equals trainer-node
+count. Global-batch scheduling on the 3T/1R case requires separate runtime and
+gradient validation; this launcher does not silently round or drop samples.
